---
// Component: SystemComparison.astro
---
<!-- DECISION GUIDE -->
<section id="comparison" class="py-20 bg-white dark:bg-slate-950 border-b border-slate-200/80 dark:border-white/10">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-14">
      <span class="text-xs font-black text-red-600 dark:text-red-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-950/50 border border-red-200 dark:border-red-800/50 shadow-2xs">
        Buyer's Technical Advice
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-3 tracking-tight font-display">
        Which Security System Suits Your Property?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        An honest technical breakdown of camera technologies, trade-offs, and practical considerations for Brisbane property owners.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      
      <!-- Card 1: Wired PoE (Recommended) -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border-2 border-red-500/80 shadow-xl shadow-red-500/5 flex flex-col justify-between relative">
        <div class="absolute -top-3.5 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 px-3.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-red-600 text-white text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider shadow-sm">
          Recommended Choice
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-950/60 text-red-700 dark:text-red-300 text-xs font-bold mb-4">
            COMMERCIAL PoE STANDARD
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2 font-display">Hardwired 4K PoE</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Continuous local recording and a dedicated solid Cat6 copper connection. Powered over Ethernet directly from the central NVR recorder.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 pt-4 mb-6">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>24/7 Continuous Recording:</strong> Never misses an event or clips seconds late.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>Immune to Wi-Fi Jammers:</strong> Solid copper cable cannot be jammed or disconnected.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>$0 Monthly Subscription:</strong> All video stored on local surveillance hard drive.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>No Batteries to Recharge:</strong> Maintenance-free operation for 10+ years.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-red-50/60 dark:bg-red-950/40 border border-red-200 dark:border-red-900/40 text-xs text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
          <strong class="font-bold text-red-700 dark:text-red-400 block font-display">Best For:</strong>
          Homeowners, detached homes, retail shops, offices, and long-term security.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 2: Wi-Fi / Battery Cameras -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-xs font-bold mb-4">
            WIRELESS ALTERNATIVE
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2 font-display">Wireless Battery Cams</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Convenient for rental properties where you cannot drill holes, but compromised by battery fatigue, wake-up lag, and ongoing subscription bills.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 pt-4 mb-6">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-amber-500 font-bold">•</span>
              <span><strong>Motion-Only Recording:</strong> Sleeps to save battery, often missing the start of incidents.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-amber-500 font-bold">•</span>
              <span><strong>Wi-Fi Vulnerability:</strong> Can be easily knocked offline by cheap signal jammers.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-amber-500 font-bold">•</span>
              <span><strong>Expensive Cloud Fees:</strong> $15–$30/month subscriptions per camera.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-amber-500 font-bold">•</span>
              <span><strong>Battery Maintenance:</strong> Must take down and recharge every 1–3 months.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          <strong class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white block font-display">Best For:</strong>
          Rental apartments and short-term leases with strict no-drilling rules.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 3: Analogue Coax Upgrades -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/60 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 text-xs font-bold mb-4">
            LEGACY RETROFIT
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2 font-display">Analogue-to-IP Upgrade</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Have an old grainy CCTV system with existing coaxial cables? We upgrade your cameras and DVR to crisp 4K without having to rewire your entire home.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 pt-4 mb-6">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>Reuses Existing Cabling:</strong> Saves money on complex multi-storey cable pulls.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>Massive Clarity Jump:</strong> Upgrade from 720p/1080p to crystal-clear 4K.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>Modern Mobile App:</strong> View feeds on iOS and Android with zero monthly fees.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>New Hardware Warranty:</strong> 3-Year replacement equipment warranty.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          <strong class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white block font-display">Best For:</strong>
          Homes and commercial buildings with existing pre-wired coax cables.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
